// docs/incidents/2026-08-03_incident_chain_reconstruction.vsm
// REPORT: [S]@S1 (DS) -> [O]@S3, per
// docs/incidents/2026-08-03_ds_dispatch_chain_reconstruction.vsm (HEAD 1654316).
// Author: DS (vsf-s1-executor), 2026-08-03.
// Gate honored: READ-ONLY investigation + writing only. No infra change, no
// service restart, no LXC start/stop/mount, no config edit, no deploy, no
// NATS/token touch. Two read-only probes (sysfs cgroup reads + repo greps)
// were used to independently verify doc claims -- nothing was mutated.
// Standing gate NOT crossed: S1-SOC-REOPEN-GATED-ON-S2S5-REVIEW.
// Scope: independent audit of the full 2026-08-01..2026-08-03 window, one
// chronological chain, one action plan, one flat checklist.

phi([S]@S1 -> [O]@S3, report) {
  ref:   docs/incidents/2026-08-03_ds_dispatch_chain_reconstruction.vsm
  scope: "48h window 2026-08-01..2026-08-03, all source material listed in the
      dispatch, plus an independent git-log + repo-wide grep pass beyond it."
  result_of_deliverable_0: "Independent pass found FOUR additional threads not
      in the dispatch's (a)-(e): (f) doc cross-reference staleness is a LIVE
      CLASS, not a closed instance; (g) repo-vs-deployed divergence on
      recovery_exercise.py after the BBS rename; (h) BBS decommission left
      repo dead code + stale docs; (i) documented 'still live' emergency cgroup
      weights do NOT match the live system. Details + evidence in
      deliverable_0 below."
  verdict_causal_chain: "NOT one single causal story: a shared physical
      substrate (single spinning disk, chronic I/O saturation) manifested as
      four separate symptoms, while THREE structurally independent failure
      classes -- (1) the 07-11 NATS-auth silent-rejection class + its
      unenforced systemic fix, (2) missing cgroup/io.max enforcement, (3)
      doc/canon staleness -- were superimposed on it. Each must be fixed as a
      class, not as the copy being looked at. Full reasoning in deliverable_1."
}

