audit(INDEPENDENT-PASS-2026-08-03) {
  method: "Read every source named in the dispatch in full, plus the full
      git log 2026-08-01..2026-08-04 (74 commits), all HANDOFF session blocks
      from the tail back through session(2026-08-02...), all TASKS.vsm ref
      strings named, and current_focus.json in full. Then ran repo-wide greps
      (not in the dispatch's list) for the same staleness classes the incident
      already documented: stale doc paths, decommissioned-component names,
      dead scripts. Two live read-only sysfs probes confirmed one claim."

  threads_found_beyond_ae: [
    "(f) DOC-CROSS-REFERENCE-STALENESS-IS-A-LIVE-CLASS — dispatch thread (e)
     closed the CLAUDE.md copy + the 4 moved docs' internal refs, but the
     class has LIVE remaining instances the same fix did not touch (verified
     by repo-wide grep, not assumption):
       - TASKS.vsm:11,118,121,125 — live header task-index still references
         docs/infrastructure.md + docs/vsm_notation_spec.md (old paths; the
         files moved to guides//spec/ months ago). A reader following task(H)
         today lands on a dead path.
       - HANDOFF.vsm.md:19 — D1 design decision @ref docs/concepts.md (dead).
       - docs/governance/security_disclosure_draft.md:219 — dead
         docs/vsm_notation_spec.md ref.
       - docs/metaphors/canonical_metaphors.md:71,296 + _en.md:67,254 — dead
         docs/concepts.md + docs/recursive_vsm_theory.md refs (live docs).
       - docs/evaluation/VSF_VSM_SCORING.md:197,308 — dead refs.
       - projects/claude-qwen-s1/example_brief.vsm:7-24 — dead docs/concepts.md
         refs in a live example brief.
       - .claude/worktrees/fix-a0-classifier-chain/ (whole checkout) — still
         carries the pre-fix state (its own copies of CLAUDE.md, README.md,
         docs with old paths). Already flagged as needing its own resync in
         nats_token_registry.vsm; the stale doc refs are the same class.
       - RULES.md:235 — historical note in `next` references the old
         docs/vsm_notation_spec.md path (acceptable as prose history, listed
         for completeness).
     CONCLUSION: the phase-C config-canon durable fix has NOT landed; the
     staleness class will recur on the next doc move. Same root pattern as
     (a)-(d): fixes applied to the copy being looked at, not the class.",

    "(g) REPO-VS-DEPLOYED DIVERGENCE AFTER THE BBS RENAME — dispatch thread
     (a) recorded that the rename sweep 'caught 4 more references incl. a
     LIVE deployed vsf-recovery-exercise gate'. The REPO copy of
     scripts/recovery_exercise.py (the source that builds that gate) still
     names the old components at lines 29-33:
       104 = s5_console + bbs-bridge + algedonic-sub
       106 = nats-server (canonical broker) + bbs-api
     Either the deployed copy was fixed in place and the repo copy never
     received the fix (repo drift), or the gate still carries stale names
     (runtime drift). This is EXACTLY the drift direction the whole incident
     documented (EnvironmentFile beats drop-in; wrapper script not in
     registry). Needs a one-line check when the next recovery exercise runs.
     NOTE: same class as STATE-DB-101-IP-CANON-MISMATCH (canon says
     .101, reality is .10) — canon-vs-reality drift, one in docs, one in
     state.db, one in a script comment.",

    "(h) BBS-DECOMMISSION-LEFT-REPO-DEAD-CODE — dispatch thread (a) recorded
     BBS 'fully decommissioned' at runtime (units removed, archived), but the
     repo still contains the poller/bridge source + docs of the dead system
     (verified by grep + ls, timestamps pre-08-02):
       - scripts/vsf_bbs_poller.py (Jul 24, 8125B) — the decommissioned n02
         host poller's repo copy.
       - scripts/bbs_decisions_bridge.py (Jul 24, 15116B) — bridge-era code.
       - docs/infra/BBS_DEPLOYMENT.md + docs/governance/bbs_whitelist_proposal.md
         — deploy/whitelist docs for a system that no longer exists.
     This is exactly the phase-C dead-code sweep target (recovery_plan.vsm
     names 'the bbs.rs removal earlier tonight is the template'), and the
     sweep has NOT happened. Low risk (nothing references them at runtime)
     but they are live instances of the 'declared done, repo still carries
     the corpse' pattern.",

    "(i) DOCUMENTED-EMERGENCY-CGROUP-WEIGHTS-DO-NOT-MATCH-LIVE — HANDOFF
     session(2026-08-02-claude-2) next[] states 'the cgroup weight changes
     made tonight (117 boosted to 800/800, clima/110-ollama/cron.service
     dropped to 20/20) are all still LIVE on n02'. Live read-only probe
     2026-08-03 (sysfs /sys/fs/cgroup/lxc/*/cpu.weight) shows ALL of
     117/112/110 at default 100, and /sys/block/sda/queue/scheduler shows
     [bfq] still active (mq-deadline was switched to bfq live on 08-02).
     Interpretation: either the weights were reverted silently (consistent
     with the documented intent 'clima and ollama probably want their normal
     priority back' after the dashboard resolved overnight) or a reboot reset
     them. Either way the DOCUMENTED state is stale — the doc claims 'still
     live' what is not live. R4-consistent: flag it, don't guess — someone
     needs to confirm whether a deliberate revert happened and whether the
     bfq scheduler switch should persist (it affects io.weight semantics
     for future thread-4 work).",

    "(j) S3-ALLOC-BASELINE-MEMORY-STALER-THAN-FLAGGED — the dispatch-named
     A0-ALLOC-BASELINE-SYNC loose end (baseline_mem 101 mismatch) is now
     WORSE: TASKS.vsm 07-02 flagged 'baseline_mem 101 8192 live vs 1024 in
     DS's tree'; the RAM-optimization pass on 2026-08-01 resized live LXC 101
     8192->3072MB (HANDOFF session 2026-08-01-claude), and the repo copy of
     scripts/s3_resource_alloc.py:115 STILL says baseline_mem 8192 for 101.
     The S3 bargain computes grants from baseline_mem; the moment the
     crash-loop is fixed, the first grant cycle would compute against a
     baseline that is 2.7x reality. This MUST land inside dispatch A before
     any grant is trusted — a NEW dependency the thermal doc did not have
     visibility into when it wrote thread_4's independence claim (the
     directive explicitly asked me to check exactly this).",

    "(k) NO-additional-threads — everything else in the 48h git log/HANDOFF
     window is accounted for by threads (a)-(j): the merkle_break
     float_roundtrip fix, VLAN20 egress root cause, jupyter VLAN40 build,
     license/covenant arc, SSD plan, corpus rescue, R15 — all independent,
     all documented in their own session blocks. The independent pass found
     no further unexamined edges beyond (f)-(j).",
  ]
}

