  chain_summary: "ONE physical substrate, THREE superimposed failure classes.
      Substrate: n02 host = single spinning sda shared by 15 LXCs, chronic
      I/O saturation (iowait 94% / load 20+ is the standing baseline). Four
      separate symptoms of it: clima's unbounded I/O (b), wazuh-db D-state
      (d1), dpkg stall (d2), NATS/106 degradation (d3) — the netdata
      correlation (disk_util 83.6%, io_some_pressure 65-75% vs 46% baseline)
      is a working explanation, [UNCERTAIN] as proven causation.
      Failure class 1 (observability/auth): the 07-11 token migration + an
      unenforced systemic fix + independently-written components (watchdog,
      wrapper script, s3-star EnvironmentFile) walking into the same silent
      rejection. This is WHY detection/delivery failed, independent of the
      disk.
      Failure class 2 (enforcement): missing cgroup cpu/memory/io.max + zero
      PSI consumers → one unit could monopolize a shared finite resource with
      no counter-mechanism. Independent of the disk (the disk made contention
      possible; the missing io.max made monopolization possible).
      Failure class 3 (doc/canon staleness): README-fix incomplete → CLAUDE.md
      dead links; token registry misses; state.db IP mismatch; repo-vs-deployed
      drift (thread g); repo dead code (thread h). Independent process failure
      that keeps producing near-misses.
      Process-level unifying theme: R4 — every claim of completeness in this
      window was a claim about the copy being looked at, not the class."

  uncertainty_flags: [
    "WHY 106 degraded at 2026-08-01T23:37-23:45 — no discrete error-level log
