       1c. STAGE2A verification follow-through: confirm the fixed watchdog
           still delivers end-to-end (it does per 08-03), monitor_reconcile
           correctness-dimension investigation (stage_2b, queued).
     DONE_WHEN: liveness scanner flags an injected flapping service; io.max
       blocks an over-consuming unit; watchdog alert lands in the ledger.",
    "STEP 2 — after this report is reviewed + dispatch A unpauses:
       2a. dispatch A (s3_resource_alloc.py bundle) — now INCLUDING thread (j)
           baseline-memory reconciliation (101: 8192 -> 3072 in the registry)
           as a mandatory first edit, before any grant is computed.
       2b. thread_4 VALIDATION under a healthy allocator: verify grants
           reallocate sanely under induced pressure + the new limits.
       2c. recovery C config centralization (ONE effort with relay decision_3):
           state.db as generative source for IP/VLAN/firewall/coupling/secrets
           config + a push mechanism generalized from rotate_nats_token.sh.
           This is the DURABLE fix for threads (e)/(f)/(g)/(h) — generated
           refs instead of hand-maintained paths.",
    "STEP 3 — design passes (dedicated sessions, not tail-end):
       3a. thermal thread_1: resolve Ax_HardwareCeiling-vs-S3-bargain scope
           question (first — determines if threads 2-3 need covenant amendment).
       3b. thermal thread_2 + recovery B2: graduated WARN->reduce-grants->
           CRITICAL ladder; wire temperature + PSI + disk-headroom as S3-bargain
           inputs (classification (b)); implement the actual wiring.
       3c. recovery B3: recalibration (Fierro Q1-Q3) after wiring changes the
           state geometry.",
    "STEP 4 — LAST, gates S1/SOC reopening:
       4a. thermal thread_3: explicit A5 ruling on emergency-kill BEFORE any
           kill-capable code (page-human-with-grace-window vs immediate-kill;
           ratified expendability priority policy — clima counterexample
           proves consumption != expendability).
       4b. recovery D: certification battery (recovery_exercise g2-g5 +
           the incident-specific tests: wrong-token reconnect, fd saturation,
           S3 bargain kill-response, algedonic end-to-end delivery under real
           induced fault) + an explicit written pass/fail threshold.
       4c. ONLY after 4b passes: reintegrate S1s (105/111/112/113/114) + SOC
           (115/116/117).",
    "STEP 5 — independent cleanup threads (each cheap, none blocking):
       5a. thread (f): sweep the ~20 stale doc-path refs (TASKS.vsm header,
           HANDOFF D1, security_disclosure_draft, canonical_metaphors, scoring,
           example_brief, worktree resync) once C's generative-ref mechanism
           exists — do NOT hand-maintain these twice.
       5b. thread (g): one-line check of deployed vs repo recovery_exercise.py;
           sync the stale topology comment.
       5c. thread (h): remove/archive scripts/vsf_bbs_poller.py +
           scripts/bbs_decisions_bridge.py + docs/infra/BBS_DEPLOYMENT.md +
           docs/governance/bbs_whitelist_proposal.md (BBS is decommissioned).
       5d. thread (i): confirm whether the cgroup-weight revert was deliberate;
           decide bfq persistence (matters for io.weight semantics).",
  ]

  sequencing_rationale: "B1+thread_4 first because both are mechanical, neither
      needs the covenant/Ω design, and thread_4 directly prevents recurrence of
      the demonstrated viability defect (b). Dispatch A next because its
      crash-loop + baseline drift (j) must be fixed before the S3 bargain can
      be trusted under the new limits. C before 3b/3c because wiring many
      signals by hand is exactly the hand-maintenance failure C exists to
      eliminate. D absolutely last — it is R14's concrete enforcement point
      and needs B/C to exist to be certified. rmw3 paces; this is the
      registration of sequence, not a commitment to start anything now."
}

